          <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Assessment and Plan"/>
          <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
          <text>
            <paragraph>Family meeting held with patient, daughter, and multidisciplinary team. Discussed patient's complex medical situation: multiple chronic conditions, polypharmacy complications, recent subdural hematoma, high fall risk, declining renal function (approaching dialysis), cognitive decline. Patient expresses frustration with multiple hospitalizations and 'too many pills.' Daughter concerned about safety at home alone. Goals of Care Discussion: Patient prioritizes quality of life over longevity. Does NOT want dialysis. Prefers to reduce medications even if it increases stroke risk. Understands risks. Decision made: 1) DISCONTINUE warfarin and clopidogrel given fall risk and ICH - accept increased stroke risk per patient wishes, 2) Simplify medication regimen focusing on symptom management, 3) Home health and PT evaluation, 4) Advance care planning - patient elects DNR/DNI status. Palliative care will continue to follow.</paragraph>
          </text>
        </section>
